{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790275659,"nonce":"OWw2yB0Q+NCE83WEYEn+mdnX5M8=","title":"Runtime reification and the compiler gaps behind haxe.macro.Printer / MacroStringTools","message":"Compiled code that uses haxe.macro (MacroStringTools, Printer) failed to compile, which failed every test importing them (TestMacro, TestMatch, Issue10744, 2958, ...). Chain of causes, all fixed:\n- `macro e` in ordinary code (MacroStringTools.toFieldExpr: `macro $i{s}`, `macro $e.$s`) reached HIR as DollarIdent. New expr/reify.rs builds the haxe.macro.Expr construction code ($i{}, $e, $name fields, calls, ops, blocks, objects, var/if/return...), laid out as the Expr typedef.\n- `pkg.Enum.Ctor` value and `pkg.Module.SubType.Ctor(args)` call did not resolve (qualified split returned \"Cannot find type\" before trying a shorter split; qualified calls handled only classes).\n- A local named function was not in scope inside closures nested in its own body (Printer's `loop`/`loopI`), and a named local function inside a function body was not bound at all.\n- Calls through a function value with missing optional args were rejected; now padded with null, and a function literal applies its parameter defaults on entry (hidden `?__opt_a`, `var a = default; if (__opt_a != null) a = __opt_a`).\n- Generic static calls with a type variable only nested in a parameter (Lambda.fold's Iterable\u003cA\u003e) were never specialized -\u003e trap stub. TAST now infers all variables (values before function literals, Iterable/Iterator typedef vs Array), static calls carry them to MIR (static_receiver path dropped them), the return type is substituted, and lambda hints resolve stdlib classes (`Lambda.fold`).\n- An object literal omitting a typedef's optional fields was laid out by its own shape when passed as an argument / array element / nested field, so reads through the typedef hit the wrong slot (was 1a5a1a8). Literals are retyped to the expected structure (through aliases, abstracts' underlying, class-registered typedefs) when they omit an optional field.\n- A typedef referenced before its declaration is a Class placeholder; MIR's resolve_through_aliases now follows it (Printer's `tpd.meta.length` was \"ambiguous field access\").\n- Object patterns inside constructors (`EMeta({name: \":implicitReturn\"}, {expr: EReturn(e1)})`) and `e.match(...)`-style sub-patterns go through the guard desugaring; object/array patterns never match null (Issue3680).\nAlso: E0803 names the function and receiver; \"unsupported expression type\" names the variant.\n\nConformance 635 -\u003e 647, 0 lost; 16 rows moved forward. Fixture: haxe-conformance/regressions/RuntimeReificationAndStructures.hx. Remaining: Printer.printExpr has a closure capture that fails to compile; ternary with a Null/Dynamic branch keeps the wrong type.","files":null}]}